cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Recall — active memory substrate for LLM agents"
message: "If you use Recall in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Recall contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/H-XX-D/recall-memory-substrate"
url: "https://github.com/H-XX-D/recall-memory-substrate"
abstract: >-
  Recall is a local-first, evidence-weighted, auditable working-memory runtime
  for LLM agents. Instead of pouring a whole store back into the prompt, an LLM
  proposes a structured write that passes an admission firewall (schema
  validation, provenance, confidence, and a rollback journal entry); memory is
  persisted as addressable graph cells and n-ary hyperedges in SQLite; and a
  context compiler returns only the relevant subgraph under a word budget. It
  ships as a single Node.js tool with a CLI, a read-only TUI, an MCP server, a
  quiet maintenance daemon, semantic search, and an encrypted secrets side
  graph.
keywords:
  - llm
  - memory
  - mcp
  - agents
  - sqlite
  - knowledge-graph
  - semantic-search
  - local-first
  - provenance
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-01"
